## 2. Environment Configuration Contracts

Each platform consumes strongly typed environment contracts backed by native build configurations (Android BuildVariants, iOS Xcode Schemes, React Native `.env` files).

<Tabs>
  <TabItem label="Android (Compose)">

```kotlin
// File: core/config/AppConfig.kt
package com.enterprise.mobile.core.config

import javax.inject.Inject
import javax.inject.Singleton

enum class EnvironmentType { DEV, STAGING, PROD }

data class AppConfig(
    val environment: EnvironmentType,
    val apiBaseUrl: String,
    val connectTimeoutSeconds: Long,
    val enableVerboseLogging: Boolean
)

@Singleton
class AppConfigProvider @Inject constructor() {
    val currentConfig: AppConfig = AppConfig(
        environment = when (BuildConfig.BUILD_TYPE) {
            "debug" -> EnvironmentType.DEV
            "staging" -> EnvironmentType.STAGING
            else -> EnvironmentType.PROD
        },
        apiBaseUrl = BuildConfig.API_BASE_URL,
        connectTimeoutSeconds = 30L,
        enableVerboseLogging = BuildConfig.DEBUG
    )
}
```

  </TabItem>
